From a6a3e0d3dea13276f62e2526152fe8c1395f9c0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:35:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Every run ends with its scorecard; one run per output folder,
 status.txt, REPL clearing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- analysis/scorecard_functions.jl, analysis/scorecard.jl: scorecard(config_file) runs every analysis that applies to
  a run (salinity drift, sea ice, mixing if arctic_mixing.jld2 exists, fastest point if monitor.csv exists, GLORYS
  transports if missing and the Tsubouchi comparison if the run overlaps their year), each in a fresh anonymous module
  (no globals reach Main) and inside try, and writes output/<experiment>/scorecard.md: settings, a headline table by
  region at the end of the run, the end-of-run rows of each table, the fastest point, the Tsubouchi blocks, and what
  ran or failed. Usable on old runs (ARGS + include) and callable as a function by a batch runner.
- run_management.jl: a RUNNING lock per output folder (atomic hard link; taken over only when its run is evidently
  gone), status.txt per run (host, GPU, state, model day, wall minutes per model day, expected end; last three lines
  for tail), clear_globals! and free_gpu_memory! (the REPL-clearing recipe), finish_run.
- panarctic.jl: clears the previous run's globals and GPU memory at the top; takes the lock before writing to the
  output folder; status at build milestones and every model hour; failures and Ctrl-C written to status.txt and the
  lock released; [output] post_run_analysis = true clears the model and runs the scorecard at the end.
- Units written Oceananigans.Units.x in panarctic.jl, setup.jl, monitor.jl, volume_control.jl; setup.jl's seconds()
  renamed elapsed_seconds.
- analysis/tsubouchi_comparison.jl brought to main's version (per-block reference θ, S of #46 with the call-site fix
  of #47): on this branch theirs() still took three arguments while 071 passed four (MethodError).
- config_smoke_test_scorecard.toml: 100 km, 1-8 Sep 2005, tanh, mixing output, post_run_analysis = true.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
